{"id":31118424933,"name":"Run api tests","node_id":"WFR_kwLOA_1uaM8AAAAHPs17ZQ","head_branch":"claude/dhis2-21947-stream-xlsx-master","head_sha":"9246ac7af78f7e55503b737423590680ac9ac422","path":".github/workflows/run-api-tests.yml","run_number":51824,"run_attempt":1,"event":"pull_request","display_title":"perf: stream the XLSX grid export instead of assembling it in heap [DHIS2-21947]","status":"completed","conclusion":"failure","workflow_id":5591308,"check_suite_id":84414896589,"check_suite_node_id":"CS_kwDOA_1uaM8AAAATp4UZzQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118424933","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118424933","created_at":"2026-08-06T16:03:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T16:30:31Z","run_started_at":"2026-08-06T16:03:09Z","jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118424933/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118424933/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/check-suites/84414896589","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118424933/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118424933/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/31118424933/rerun","head_commit":{"message":"perf: stream the XLSX grid export instead of assembling it in heap [DHIS2-21947]\n\nGridUtils.toXlsx built the whole workbook as live POI objects before writing a\nbyte. On Uganda's 100 001-row trackedEntities line-list export that was 19.9% of\nthe request's CPU - 160 of 803 profile samples in cell creation and\nworkbook.write - and a large share of the 132 GB it allocated. The cleanest\nisolation is in the traces themselves: four of the five requests were .xlsx and one\nwas .xml, same query and same 100 001 rows, and the final phase after the last\ndatabase entry was 51.1 s against 14.3 s. About 37 s of each xlsx request was\nspreadsheet serialisation on a grid that was already built.\n\ntoXlsx now writes through an SXSSFWorkbook with a 1 000-row window, so peak memory\nis a function of the row width rather than of the result size. Nothing in this path\nreads a row back after writing it, which is the one thing the streaming API cannot\ndo, and toXls stays on HSSFWorkbook - the streaming API is XSSF-only and the legacy\nformat's 65 536-row ceiling makes it moot.\n\nMeasured over a 20-column grid, peak heap taken above a post-GC baseline captured\nonce the grid was built, so what is reported is the workbook and not the grid:\n\n   25 000 rows   before 15 680 ms / 1 165 MB      after 3 514 ms / 207 MB\n   50 000 rows   before OOM-killed                after 3 839 ms /  93 MB\n  100 000 rows   before OOM-killed                after 5 422 ms / 410 MB\n\nAt Uganda's actual export size the old path does not complete in an 8 GB container\nat all. The 25 000-row pair is the comparable one: 4.5x faster, 5.6x less peak heap.\n\nThe spilled rows are real files under the temp directory. toWorkbook closes the\nworkbook on the happy path, but a write that fails part-way - a broken pipe, which\nis precisely how all five traced requests ended - must not leave them behind, so\ndispose runs in a finally. A test asserts that, and asserts POI's spill directory\nexists first so the assertion cannot pass vacuously. A second test reads the bytes\nback and pins the sheet name, title and subtitle rows, header row, cell types and\nboth number formats.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","author":{"name":"Stian Sandvold","email":"stian@dhis2.org"},"id":"9246ac7af78f7e55503b737423590680ac9ac422","tree_id":"f52c6846b33f922d030965219f1493592eabc8ff","timestamp":"2026-08-06T12:46:33Z","committer":{"name":"stian-sandvold","email":"stian@dhis2.org"}},"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/workflows/5591308","repository":{"id":66940520,"node_id":